--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bpod (Sanworks LLC) — an intellectual ancestor, NOT a code ancestor
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bpod <https://sanworks.io> (Sanworks LLC, Josh Sanders, out of the Kepecs
lab) is the direct intellectual ancestor of the model implemented here. The
idea of a state matrix as the per-trial unit of configuration is Bpod's, and
`dev/PLAN.md` sets out at length what we take from it and what we do
differently.

**No Bpod source code is copied, translated or adapted in this repository.**
Every reference to Bpod in these sources is a comment comparing our design to
theirs — usually to explain a deliberate divergence, such as sparse per-state
transition lists in place of Bpod's dense [state][event] matrix, three-mask
conditions over the whole input word in place of its one-channel/one-value
Condition, and a foreground scan in place of its in-ISR state machine.

Consequently no file here carries a Sanworks copyright line, and this
project's GPLv3 licensing is a deliberate choice to stay compatible with the
system it takes its ideas from, rather than an obligation inherited by
copying its code. Should any Bpod source later be incorporated, that file
must carry the Sanworks copyright notice alongside ours and this section must
be amended to say which file and what was taken.

